<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teodoro de Croix</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1730–<a href="/years/1792">1792</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teodoro de Croix (1730–1792) was a Flemish-born officer in Spanish service who became the first commandant general of the Internal Provinces of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> in 1776. He reorganised the frontier presidios and the defence against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apache">Apache</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> raids. He was later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1784 to 1790.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teodoro-de-croix.jpg" alt="Teodoro de Croix" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teodoro_de_Croix.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
